    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="badge">Open source &middot; Apache-2.0 &middot; written in Rust</p>
          <h1>A fast coding agent that gets work done.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Use Cook from your terminal with the CLI or in <strong>Let Cook</strong>, the desktop
            app for Windows, macOS, and Ubuntu. It runs on your machine with your own API keys.
          </p>

          <div class="cmd" data-curl-cta>
            <code id="install-command">curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | bash</code>
            <button
              class="copy-btn"
              type="button"
              data-copy
              data-copy-label="install command"
              data-copy-text="curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | bash"
            >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="cmd" data-windows-cta hidden>
            <span class="cmd-text">
              Download the CLI binary here, or choose the Windows desktop installer below.
            </span>
            <a class="copy-btn" data-asset="cli" href="https://download.letcook.dev/cook-1.0.37-windows-x86_64">
              Download
            </a>
          </div>

          <p class="fine">
            macOS, Linux, and Windows &middot;
            <a href="#install">download an installer instead</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="speed">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Fast from the first command</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Cook is a native Rust binary built to start quickly and keep every turn moving.
          </p>
          <ul class="lines">
            <li>
              <strong>Starts in milliseconds.</strong>
              No Node, no Python, no JVM. <code>cook</code> is a single Rust binary on your
              <code>PATH</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Keeps work moving.</strong>
              Streaming, tool calls, and subagents overlap in one runtime instead of waiting in a
              queue.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>A lightweight desktop app.</strong>
              Let Cook uses Tauri and the system webview instead of bundling a browser.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="configure">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Make Cook yours</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Set up your models, skills, commands, and permissions with simple files.
          </p>
          <ul class="lines">
            <li><strong>Models.</strong> Connect your preferred provider and use your own API keys.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Skills and commands.</strong> Add reusable instructions and shortcuts without
              changing the code.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Permissions.</strong> Choose what Cook can read, run, and write.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="install">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Get Cook running</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            On macOS or Linux, one command installs the CLI and desktop app. Download the desktop
            app for Windows, macOS, or Ubuntu below.
          </p>

          <div class="cmd">
            <code>curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | bash</code>
            <button
              class="copy-btn"
              type="button"
              data-copy
              data-copy-label="install command"
              data-copy-text="curl -fsSL https://download.letcook.dev/install.sh | bash"
            >
              Copy
            </button>
          </div>

          <h3>Desktop app</h3>
          <ul class="downloads">
            <li>
              <a data-asset="mac-arm" href="https://download.letcook.dev/v1.0.37/let-cook-1.0.37-macos-aarch64.dmg">macOS &middot; Apple Silicon</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a data-asset="mac-intel" href="https://download.letcook.dev/v1.0.37/let-cook-1.0.37-macos-x86_64.dmg">macOS &middot; Intel</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a data-asset="linux-appimage" href="https://download.letcook.dev/v1.0.37/let-cook-1.0.37-linux-x86_64.AppImage">Linux &middot; AppImage</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a data-asset="linux" href="https://download.letcook.dev/v1.0.37/let-cook-1.0.37-linux-x86_64.deb">Ubuntu &middot; .deb</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a data-asset="windows" href="https://download.letcook.dev/v1.0.37/let-cook-1.0.37-windows-x86_64-setup.exe">Windows &middot; installer</a>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>CLI</h3>
          <ul class="downloads">
            <li>
              <a data-asset="cli" href="https://download.letcook.dev/cook-1.0.37-macos-aarch64">CLI binary &middot; <span data-cli-platform>macos-aarch64</span></a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
